# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build.
#
# This file's existence matters as much as its contents. Without it, gcloud
# falls back to .gitignore - which excludes `dist/`, the one directory the
# image actually needs. The build would then succeed, push an image with no
# frontend in it, and serve 404s at the root with nothing in the logs to
# explain why.
#
# Size is the other reason. The build context moved to the repo root so the
# Dockerfile could reach frontend/dist, which pulled in .venv (231 MB),
# node_modules (9 MB) and the data cache (23 MB) - 3,882 files and 44 MiB,
# enough that archiving it crashed on Windows with a file-locking error.

# Dependencies - reinstalled inside the image, never shipped
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Pipeline data belongs in the bucket DATA_DIR points at. Baking a snapshot
# into the image would serve stale results no pipeline run could refresh.
backend/data/

# Airflow runtime output
backend/logs/
backend/plugins/
backend/config/
backend/airflow.db

# Local tooling
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
backend/tests/

# Secrets - must never reach a build layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Docs are not needed to build or run
*.md
